From 5abef5b5053be290650438f9921a68b602f41547 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:40:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] feat(floor-studio): the design travels, and the visitor
 does not retype it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FS-05 of the Floor Studio series.

lib/design-config.ts says its key is versioned, that a shape change must
bump it, and that old data must never be reinterpreted. That instruction
is followed literally: ew-design-v1 IS NOT TOUCHED. Floor Studio writes a
second, richer record under ew-studio-v1 AND keeps writing the v1 record,
so every existing consumer — EstimateForm's chip, /design/spec, the
querystring contract, the copies of ew-design-v1 already sitting in
people's browsers — keeps working with no migration.

NO PRICE IS EVER STORED

A saved design carries the configuration, the area, the feels and the
three facts the photo yielded. Never the range. A stored number is a price
frozen at the moment somebody clicked save, and the first time the rate
table moves, a share link from three weeks ago quotes a figure this
business no longer stands behind — to a stranger, with our name on it. A
test asserts the persisted record has no price-shaped field other than the
budget the VISITOR typed.

THE SHARE CODE IS READABLE ON PURPOSE

c=white-oak.satin.herringbone.5&a=900&f=warmer,natural rather than a
base64 blob. A support call can read it down the phone; a crawler can see
these URLs are parameterisations of one page; and anybody auditing what we
persist can read it without a decoder. Every field is validated against
the catalogue on the way back in — a link naming a floor we do not lay
resolves to null, not to a render of something unbuyable. Unknown feels
are dropped rather than failing the whole link.

THE PHOTOGRAPH IS NOT IN IT. A share link carries a floor and a number of
square feet. The image never leaves the device that took it.

THE ESTIMATE FORM NOW RECEIVES STRUCTURE, NOT A PARAGRAPH

leadSchema gains `design` (the code, max 400 chars, unknown keys still
stripped). /api/leads appends it to the note verbatim rather than
re-rendering it into prose — a second description of a floor in a file
that knows nothing about the catalogue is how two surfaces start
describing the same floor differently. EstimateForm reads ?design= on
mount, and when a link and a stored v1 config disagree the LINK wins:
somebody who followed a link is looking at the floor in that link, not at
what they configured on this device last month. The chip shows the
FS-XXXXXXX reference and links back to the studio, because the first thing
a person does with a reference is want to see it.

24 tests here; 449 across the app. pnpm verify green (66 guards).
tsc --noEmit is unchanged: the only errors in this sandbox are the
pre-existing ones from @prisma/client, which cannot be generated here
because binaries.prisma.sh is unreachable — the same constraint
verify-client-boundary.mjs was written for.

